SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast A Dress Rehearsal – ACT II Cast A (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 7:30 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 7:15 PM.\nOn stage: 8:10 PM–8:50 PM.\nACT II
  Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — p
 roduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time dan
 cers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Ti
 me.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgi
 ving and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are ca
 lled unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedu
 le\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mas
 ter: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-
 N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Archangels ***\nAng
 els - Archangels — Costume (you provide): Pink Seamless Tights\, Flesh
 -tone camisole leotard\; Shoes: Pink Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Full Stage M
 akeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\nFull Stage Makeup Instruction Sheet:\n
 • Apply foundation and powder matching skintone\n• Light skin tone e
 ye shadow over entire eye\n• Dark brown eye shadow over crease\n• Me
 dium brown eye shadow blended over brown\n• Black fake eyelashes (note
 : apply mascara to own lashes before application of fake lashes)\n• Ap
 ply eyeliner after lashes dry\n• Blush on the cheeks (be sure to apply
  plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lights)\n• Br
 own or tan on contour cheekbones\, hairline\n• Use a brow pencil (or e
 yeshadow) to darken the eyebrows\n• Red or Dark Red Lipstick\nDancers 
 of Color may wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostum
 e Care Guidelines:\n• Handle costume pieces with care while changing t
 o prevent damage to delicate fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansa
 s in the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter h
 ow significant\n• Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, o
 r hang costumes by their elastic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the
  floor while in costume\n• Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or
  launder any costume or accessory\n• Never apply stage make-up while i
 n costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging make-up on 
 costume during its removal\n• Refrain from the use of spray perfume or
  cologne while in costume\n• Never wear any garment not assigned to ca
 st member\n• Do not handle or consume food or beverage while in costum
 e\, with the exception of water\n• Do not remove costumes from their a
 ssigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins us
 ed to secure head pieces and wigs following their use\n• Return all he
 adpieces to their assigned bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updat
 es to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, pa
 ints\, colored drinks or anything that may damage or stain costumes.
